    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Traversal to insert a new global prototype.</para><para>This traversal searches for the first non-defining declaration for a given function definition, and inserts a new prototype of that function into global scope. In addition, it fixes up the definition&apos;s first non-defining declaration field to point to the new global prototype.</para><para>The traversal terminates as soon as the first matching declaration is found by throwing an exception as a string encoded with the word &quot;done&quot;. The caller must ensure that any other matching declarations have their first non-defining declaration fields fixed up as well. </para>    </detaileddescription>
